import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'undead':('A healthy bat and a nearly-dead one','A level-14 Necromancer with both books faces a healthy vampire bat five grids away and a vampire bat hurt to a fifth of its hp three grids away; a wall sits just beyond each. The original rates the tap at each target\'s full hp, so it taps toward the healthy bat; the correction rates both taps at real damage, where the nearly-dead bat rates higher, and taps toward it.'),
 'non-undead':('Control: only a plain giant','With only a hill giant in sight the tap rates zero in both versions and the Nether Bolt is cast. The complete logs are byte-identical.'),
 'bat':('Control: only one healthy bat','With only one bat in sight the tap wins in both versions — after the correction on real damage alone, before on the inflated rating. The decision and the complete logs are byte-identical.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/tapunlife-249 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw}
  for tag,key in (('SETUP level=','setup'),('DECISION ','decision'),('OUTCOME ','outcome')):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[key]={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])} if match else None
  seq=re.search(r'sequence=(.*)',raw)
  entry['sequence']=seq[1].strip() if seq else None
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Tap Unlife rated by the target's full hit points</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native Tap Unlife decisions</p><h1>Tap Unlife was rated at the target's full hit points</h1><p>The Borg's Tap Unlife case computes its mana gain as current mana minus current mana — always zero — so the spell's rating falls through to the monster's full estimated hp. Any undead therefore looks like a one-shot worth finishing, and the borg prefers a full-health undead over one it could actually finish with the same free cast. The correction rates the tap at its real damage, like the other dispel cases, and ignores the mana gain as the code comment already says.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">The target list</button><button data-step="1">The decision</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the controls establish</h2><p>With only the plain giant, both versions cast the bolt; with only the small bat, both versions cast the tap. Those two complete logs match byte for byte, so the correction changes nothing except the huge-undead case.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Necromancer level 14, depth 30, seed 1000, glowing constructed arena, both shadow books ([Into the Shadows], [Dark Rituals]), Nether Bolt and Tap Unlife learned, full mana and hp, no light source (a necromancer's fail rate rises by 25 on a lit square). The production attack chooser acts on its own filled target list; the cast is shown by its queued keys, not executed. This isolates the tap rating, not full autonomous play; no damage or survival claim.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/249">issue249</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=1;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}
function castLabel(c){if(!c)return'No decision recorded';return c.outcome&&c.outcome.tap_cast?'Casts Tap Unlife':(c.outcome&&c.outcome.acted?'Casts Nether Bolt':'Casts nothing')}
function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.num').textContent=step===0?`Targets: ${c.label.startsWith('Control')?'one monster':'two bats'} within range.`:castLabel(d);p.querySelector('.state').textContent=step===0?'Each bat is in line of sight with a wall just beyond it.':'The chooser queues its chosen spell keys.';p.querySelector('.action').textContent=step===1?`Queued: ${d.sequence||'none'} (${d.outcome?d.outcome.keys:0} keys).`:'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}
document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='undead'?'The original taps toward the healthy bat because the tap is rated at its full hp; the correction rates the tap at real damage and taps toward the nearly-dead bat.':'Both versions agree in this control; the logs match byte for byte.';for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}
select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=1;draw()});for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
